      <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal> Sealing your house will help improve the energy saving of your home. To achieve better result a house wrap is the best solution to fix all cracks and air infiltration penetrating in the residence.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>At the time of the assessment, the insulation of the exterior walls was R-12. We recommend upgrading the insulation level. You are eligible for $2.50/square foot for the addition of R-20+, and $ 3.50/square foot for R-30+. </mainWalls>
                <ceilings>At the time of the audit, the insulation level of the attic was estimated to be R-20. We recommend adding insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse standard of R-60.</ceilings>
                <foundation>At the time of the audit no insulation was observed on the foundation walls. We strongly recommend adding insulation on the foundation walls. Insulating the basement will contribute directly to energy savings.  </foundation>
                <windows>We recommend the replacement of the windows by triple pane and Energy Star certified units with Lowe coating and Argon filled.</windows>
                <doors>We recommend the replacement of the wood doors with new energy star certified products.  </doors>
                <VentilationSystem>We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) and Energy Star certified, to ensure proper ventilation inside your home.</VentilationSystem>
            </RURComments>
      <GreenerHomes basementSlabInsulated="false" moistureProofCrawlSpace="false" waterproofing="false" roofingMembrane="false" minR10ContinuousExposedFloors="false" backwaterValve="false" sumpPump="false" smartThermostats="false" remoteCommunities="false" evaluationCost="">
